 @Trisstan20  I owned the OG ATI Radeon 9700 PRO that showed Nvidia who was boss and I never had any of "the many fabled driver issues". I do, however, remember that my RX 580 sometimes took a week or two to get a driver fix for the less hyped games during AMD's worst financials. But by the time I replaced it with a 6700XT it was absolutely mint. My 7900XTX blows the tires off in every respect.

I also owned an Intel i740 which was the worst experience of anything I've ever owned. My old S3 Virge was better than that POS. It does, however, look like Intel is planning to stick with it this time and has hired a driver team that knows what they're doing. Doesn't change the fact that it takes literal years to build a solid driver stack when you need to support several versions of OpenGL, Vulkan, DirectX, OpenCL and their own OneAPI stuff.

What's interesting, though, is that Hardware Unboxed just casually mentioned in passing that lately they've had less trouble with AMD drivers than with Nvidia's drivers.
